---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';
---

<PageLayout
  title="How We Use Data"
  description="Exactly what ContextLife does and does not do with your data — including the assessment, analytics, and any future advertising."
  path="/how-we-use-data"
  eyebrow="Trust & Legal"
  heading="How we use data."
  lede="A plain-language companion to our privacy policy: what happens to your information, in specifics."
  updated="June 2026"
>
  <h2>Your assessment answers</h2>
  <p>
    The Context Assessment is computed entirely in your browser using JavaScript.
    When you answer a question, the value is held in memory on your device and used
    to generate the context shown on the results screen. That is the whole journey.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>No server submission.</strong> Answers are never sent to us.</li>
    <li><strong>No storage.</strong> We do not save them to a database, cookies, or local storage.</li>
    <li><strong>No identity.</strong> We never ask who you are, so answers cannot be tied to you.</li>
    <li><strong>No persistence.</strong> Closing or refreshing the page erases them.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>If we ever add submissions</h2>
  <p>
    We may, in the future, let people optionally contribute anonymised, aggregated
    answers to improve the population context we show — for example, to display how
    other visitors answered a question. If we ever do this, it will be
    <strong>strictly opt-in</strong>, clearly explained at the point of collection,
    fully anonymised, and never required to use the tool. We will update this page
    before any such feature launches.
  </p>

  <h2>Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    To understand which pages are useful, we may use privacy-respecting analytics.
    When enabled, analytics measure <strong>aggregate, anonymised</strong> usage —
    page views, rough visitor counts, general device and region information. They do
    not capture your assessment answers, and we do not attempt to identify
    individuals. Analytics are off unless explicitly enabled, and we honour browser
    "Do Not Track" and consent signals where applicable.
  </p>

  <h2>Advertising</h2>
  <p>
    The site currently shows no ads. If we introduce Google AdSense after approval,
    advertising partners may use cookies to show relevant ads, governed by their own
    policies. We will:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Keep ads clearly labelled and never disguise them as content, navigation, or research findings.</li>
    <li>Never place ads inside the assessment or its results.</li>
    <li>Request consent for non-essential cookies where the law requires it.</li>
    <li>Update our <a href="/privacy-policy">privacy policy</a> to describe exactly what changes.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What we will never do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Sell your personal information.</li>
    <li>Store or share your assessment answers.</li>
    <li>Require an account to use the core tool.</li>
    <li>Collect sensitive personal data we do not need.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>
    If anything here is unclear, email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
    See also our <a href="/privacy-policy">privacy policy</a>.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
